2026-09-23T13:53:26.5069018Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5069509Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5069909Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5070111Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5070366Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5070693Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5070929Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071139Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071410Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071509Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071593Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071670Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071767Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071864Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5071941Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072025Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072117Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072229Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072321Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072499Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072600Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072677Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072776Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5072859Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073005Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073181Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073262Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073359Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073458Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073558Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073657Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073735Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5073854Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5074011Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5074088Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5074284Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5075050Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5075131Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5075210Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5075297Z     Features
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5075387Z     --------
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5075462Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5075937Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5076121Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5076218Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5076512Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5076618Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5076700Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5076964Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5077133Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5077214Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5077474Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5077572Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5077652Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5077753Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5077830Z     
2026-09-23T13:53:26.5078316Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
